Vanilla crème brûlée
6
Creamy vanilla crème brûlée, topped with brown sugar crust.

---
Crème brûlée
egg yolks|8|pcs
semi-skimmed milk|400|ml
double cream|400|ml
vanilla pods|2|pcs
powdered sugar|100|g

Topping
brown sugar|20|g

---
Preheat the oven to 100°C.
Bring the milk and cream to the boil with the split and scraped vanilla pods.
Whisk the egg yolks with the sugar vigorously.
Pour the hot vanilla milk and cream over the yolks while whisking.
Divide the mixture among crème brûlée ramekins.
Bake in a dry oven at 100°C for 40 min to 1 hour, until set but still wobbly in the centre.
Let cool then refrigerate.

To serve, sprinkle the surface with brown sugar.
Caramelise with a blowtorch or under the grill until you have a thin golden crust.

---
Cook the custards in a bain-marie on the stove over low heat for about 20 min.
Avoid overcooking to keep a creamy texture.

---
dessert
creme-brulee
vanilla
cream
